 34AR    COULOMB EXCITATION            2023DR01                  ENSDF    202609
 34AR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AR c  2023Dr01: An intermediate Coulomb excitation experiment was performed  
 34AR2c  to measure the B(E2, 0{++}{-1} |) 2{++}{-1}) value of {+36,38}Ca.      
 34AR3c  {+34}Ar beam was a contaminant produced from the fragmentation of a 140
 34AR4c  MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca primary beam delivered by the Coupled Cyclotron    
 34AR5c  Facility at the National Superconducting Cyclotron Laboratory (NSCL)   
 34AR6c  impinging upon an 800 mg/cm{+2} thick {+9}Be production target and     
 34AR7c  separated using a 300 mg/cm{+2} Al wedge degrader in the A1900 fragment
 34AR8c  separator. Secondary beam was scattered off a 257 mg/cm{++2} thick Au  
 34AR9c  foil located at the target position of the S800 spectrograph. The      
 34ARAc  deexcited |g-rays were detected using GRETINA surrounded S800          
 34ARBc  spectrograph. The GRETINA consisted a total of 48 HPGe crystals; 32 of 
 34ARCc  them at 90|' and 16 of them at 58|' with respect to the beam direction.
 34ARDc  The inelastic excitations of the projectile and target nuclei were     
 34AREc  quantified with the detection of prompt |g-rays in GRETINA. The        
 34ARFc  scattered projectiles were identified using S800 focal plane detection 
 34ARGc  system together with tof measurement. Measured: E|g, tof, cross section
 34ARHc  and B(E2). Comparison with the shell model calculations.               
 34AR cL E$From measured E|g (2023Dr01).                                        
 34AR cL J$From the Adopted Levels.                                             
